    "text": "<div>Given line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></math></div><div>Given circles&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>According to the given information centres of both the circles must lie on opposite side of line.</div><div><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>11</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>22</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#60;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>27</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8712;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>31</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></mfenced></math>.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Line is neither touching nor intersecting that means perpendicular distance from&nbsp; centre to line must more than or equal to radius.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</